# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state and build output.
# approach2/docker_scripts/run/ is ~491 MB of pure runtime artefacts:
#   run/stratum/write-reqs.txt  P4Runtime write log (259 MB and growing)
#   run/logs/                   service logs (231 MB)
#   run/build/                  Maven sandbox used by 06_deploy_app.sh
# target/ is Maven output. It was tracked upstream, which is why 06_deploy_app.sh
# builds out-of-tree (mvn clean would delete tracked files). Untracked here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
approach2/docker_scripts/run/
approach2/onos_app/approach2/target/

# Dependencies
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Vendored third-party build tree (~130 MB of source + cmake objects).
# UERANSIM.zip is tracked in the repo, so this is reconstructible.
UERANSIM/

# Attack captures from the StopDDoS collection. Their licence permits use for
# building DDoS protection but grants no redistribution, so fetch them instead:
#   tools/fetch_stopddos.sh
# datasets/samples/ is our own synthetic sample and IS committed.
datasets/stopddos/
datasets/*.pcap
datasets/*.pcapng

# Experiment run logs. The results CSVs and the small evidence pcaps
# (expD_n7.pcap, expD_pfcp.pcap) are kept.
experiments/*/results/*.log

# Local session notes: contains pasted terminal transcripts including
# "[sudo] password for herman". Do not publish.
/5G-SDN-DDoS-Detection-Mitigation *.md
